Tokenization :Tokenization is the process of breaking down raw text (a sentence, paragraph, or document) into smaller, manageable chunks called tokens.
These tokens can be words, subwords (pieces of words), or individual characters, depending on the tokenizer (e.g., Byte-Pair Encoding used by modern LLMs).

Encoding:Once you have the tokens, the model passes them through a vocabulary dictionary to map each token to a unique integer ID.
